<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">José Antonio Páez</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1790–1873</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">José Antonio Páez was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>-plains leader whose llanero cavalry fought for Venezuelan independence under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a>, winning at Las Queseras del Medio in 1819 and sharing the victory of Carabobo in 1821. Commanding in Venezuela within <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esztergom">Gran</a> Colombia, he led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-cosiata">Cosiata</a> revolt of 1826 and the secession of 1830. He was Venezuela's first president and dominated its politics for decades, ending his life in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jose-antonio-paez.jpg" alt="José Antonio Páez" width="320" height="448" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John J. Peoli · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_J._Peoli_-_General_Jose_Antonio_Paez_-_1910.10.4_-_Smithsonian_American_Art_Museum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
